00:00:15.905 --> 00:00:19.219
♪ But you take up half this bed ♪

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:22.122
♪ You're livin' rent-free in my head ♪

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:26.496
♪ Oh, insecurity ♪

00:00:26.496 --> 00:00:28.757
♪ You show up in my mirror ♪

00:00:28.757 --> 00:00:33.034
♪ Point out the worst in me ♪

00:00:33.034 --> 00:00:36.116
♪ You whisper in my ear ♪

00:00:36.116 --> 00:00:39.232
♪ That my lips are way too thin ♪

00:00:39.232 --> 00:00:43.368
♪ Too many miles on my skin ♪

00:00:43.368 --> 00:00:48.368
♪ If I can't find a way to get you gone ♪

00:00:49.984 --> 00:00:54.984
♪ Can we find a way to
get along, along, along ♪

00:00:56.768 --> 00:01:01.768
♪ You're careless, and you're
cruel, and oh, you're mindless ♪

00:01:03.338 --> 00:01:08.338
♪ Maybe you could try a little kindness ♪

00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:12.992
♪ Instead of hurtin' me ♪

00:01:12.992 --> 00:01:17.285
♪ 'Cause insecurity ♪

00:01:17.285 --> 00:01:19.471
♪ This time feels like love ♪

00:01:19.471 --> 00:01:23.717
♪ She's really sure of me ♪

00:01:23.717 --> 00:01:26.853
♪ So, please don't mess this up ♪

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:29.498
♪ If you cut in on this dance ♪

00:01:29.498 --> 00:01:33.498
♪ I may never get another chance ♪

00:01:33.498 --> 00:01:38.498
♪ I'll never find a way to get you gone ♪

00:01:40.111 --> 00:01:45.111
♪ Wish I could find a way to
know you're wrong, you're wrong ♪

00:01:46.842 --> 00:01:51.842
♪ You're careless, and you're
cruel, and oh, you're mindless ♪

00:01:53.464 --> 00:01:56.547
♪ Maybe you could try a little kindness ♪

00:01:59.343 --> 00:02:02.990
♪ Instead of hurtin' me ♪
♪ Instead of hurtin' me ♪

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:06.596
♪ Why you hurtin' me ♪

00:02:06.596 --> 00:02:07.429
♪ Insecurity ♪

00:02:09.705 --> 00:02:13.354
(gentle piano music)

00:02:13.354 --> 00:02:14.479
(audience applauds)

00:02:14.479 --> 00:02:16.012
- Best songwriter of our generation.

00:02:16.012 --> 00:02:16.845
Give it up!

00:02:16.845 --> 00:02:18.403
(audience applauds)

00:02:18.403 --> 00:02:19.236
(indistinct)

00:02:19.236 --> 00:02:20.669
(Kelly claps)

00:02:20.669 --> 00:02:22.295
(audience applauding)

00:02:22.295 --> 00:02:24.245
(indistinct)

00:02:24.245 --> 00:02:26.745
Welcome to "The Kelly
Clarkson Show", everybody.

00:02:26.745 --> 00:02:27.781
Give it up for my band, y'all,

00:02:27.781 --> 00:02:31.695
and my wonderful, extraordinary
duet partner, Brandi Clark.

00:02:31.695 --> 00:02:35.525
(audience applauds)

00:02:35.525 --> 00:02:38.328
That was her single, "Dear Insecurity",

00:02:38.328 --> 00:02:40.728
off her new self-titled album.

00:02:40.728 --> 00:02:42.145
Grammy nominated.

00:02:43.481 --> 00:02:44.346
(audience cheers)

00:02:44.346 --> 00:02:46.082
She recorded it with Brandi Carlile.

00:02:46.082 --> 00:02:47.746
It's Brandi's Squared event.

00:02:47.746 --> 00:02:50.189
I am so honored she let
me sing on it with her.

00:02:50.189 --> 00:02:51.490
I'm a huge fan.

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:53.613
All I do is word vomit
every time I'm around her

00:02:53.613 --> 00:02:54.446
'cause I'm such a fan.

00:02:54.446 --> 00:02:56.269
But I literally think that you are

00:02:56.269 --> 00:02:58.125
the greatest songwriter of our generation.

00:02:58.125 --> 00:02:59.708
You're so talented.

